1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
What if theatre were not a building,

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,367
a company, or a finished play,

3
00:00:03,367 --> 00:00:05,767
but a method for making relations visible?

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,800
P4 Theater is an independent experimental

5
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,133
theatre and public practice project founded

6
00:00:18,133 --> 00:00:22,200
in Beijing in 2015 by Zhang Shaohua and He Fa.

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:24,667
It is not simply a troupe, a venue,

8
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:27,067
or a repertory of finished productions.

9
00:00:27,067 --> 00:00:31,000
P4 uses theatre to organize live situations.

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,200
People enter,

11
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,400
roles shift,

12
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,867
relations become visible,

13
00:00:34,867 --> 00:00:37,167
and the encounter leaves a record.

14
00:00:37,167 --> 00:00:39,100
Performance, photography,

15
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,067
moving image,

16
00:00:40,067 --> 00:00:42,267
public writing and participation

17
00:00:42,267 --> 00:00:44,233
operate within one system.

18
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:48,800
In P4,

19
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,900
The work does not begin when the lights

20
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:53,200
go down or end with applause.

21
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:55,933
A project may start with a public invitation,

22
00:00:55,933 --> 00:00:57,933
bring strangers into a workshop,

23
00:00:57,933 --> 00:01:00,233
turn rehearsal into collective research,

24
00:01:00,233 --> 00:01:01,667
produce a performance,

25
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:04,567
record disagreements and audience responses,

26
00:01:04,567 --> 00:01:06,733
publish photographs and essays,

27
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:08,067
then use that archive

28
00:01:08,067 --> 00:01:09,767
to generate the next project.

29
00:01:09,767 --> 00:01:10,800
The invitation,

30
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:12,567
rehearsal, argument,

31
00:01:12,567 --> 00:01:14,333
camera, aftertalk

32
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:16,700
essay, and hard drive can all

33
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,267
belong to the same event.

34
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,600
P4's current history begins in 2015.

35
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:34,867
Its public opening is documented in 2016

36
00:01:34,867 --> 00:01:37,933
inside Beijing's Sculpture Studio Art Zone,

37
00:01:37,933 --> 00:01:40,100
where an artist's photographic studio

38
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:43,133
was rebuilt as an independent black box.

39
00:01:43,367 --> 00:01:45,167
Early records describe a room

40
00:01:45,167 --> 00:01:47,900
divided by black velvet into black and white

41
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:50,733
zones with space for roughly 80 people

42
00:01:50,733 --> 00:01:53,467
and a stage about 10 meters wide.

43
00:01:53,767 --> 00:01:55,433
The first public performance,

44
00:01:55,433 --> 00:01:56,867
Shadow Counterpoint,

45
00:01:56,867 --> 00:02:00,800
was co devised by Ao Shuang and He Fa.

46
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:03,133
Projected images, sound,

47
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:05,600
repeated instructions, bodies,

48
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:07,267
cameras and spectators

49
00:02:07,267 --> 00:02:08,900
were placed in relation.

50
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:11,333
From the beginning, P4 was designing

51
00:02:11,333 --> 00:02:12,933
encounters across media.

52
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
The name began with a photographic question.

53
00:02:17,433 --> 00:02:20,733
P4 could be heard as photo for you,

54
00:02:20,733 --> 00:02:23,700
but you meant the person beneath the pose

55
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:26,333
encountered through reciprocal looking.

56
00:02:26,333 --> 00:02:30,433
In 2016, the four P’s were Present,

57
00:02:30,433 --> 00:02:33,933
Photosynthesis, Psychology, and Permanent.

58
00:02:33,933 --> 00:02:35,533
Psychology was an artistic

59
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:37,367
catalyst for attention and relation,

60
00:02:37,367 --> 00:02:39,167
not a clinical claim.

61
00:02:39,533 --> 00:02:42,167
The early logo showed two rotating figures,

62
00:02:42,167 --> 00:02:44,800
each watching and reshaping the other.

63
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,700
That reciprocal structure remains

64
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:48,400
more important than any single

65
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,933
expansion of the letters.

66
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,733
That photographic origin became

67
00:02:58,733 --> 00:03:00,200
a three-part method:

68
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:02,667
look, perform, shoot.

69
00:03:02,667 --> 00:03:04,833
Looking is not passive judgement;

70
00:03:04,833 --> 00:03:06,433
it is an encounter.

71
00:03:06,433 --> 00:03:08,367
Performing produces a temporary

72
00:03:08,367 --> 00:03:10,933
reality shared by everyone present.

73
00:03:10,933 --> 00:03:13,400
Shooting is not neutral documentation.

74
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:15,167
The camera chooses a position,

75
00:03:15,167 --> 00:03:17,467
participates, and turns a fleeting

76
00:03:17,467 --> 00:03:20,533
relation into evidence for a future viewer.

77
00:03:20,833 --> 00:03:22,133
Real Image:

78
00:03:22,133 --> 00:03:25,900
Eight and a Half made this explicit in 2019,

79
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:27,333
turning portrait making

80
00:03:27,333 --> 00:03:30,000
into one to one photographic theatre.

81
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,733
Across linked encounters,

82
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:33,833
Photographing, looking,

83
00:03:33,833 --> 00:03:35,667
speaking, and responding

84
00:03:35,667 --> 00:03:38,067
became part of the performance.

85
00:03:38,067 --> 00:03:40,233
Participants chose whether to continue

86
00:03:40,233 --> 00:03:42,833
and whether their images could be made public.

87
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,500
From late 2020, participation

88
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,333
became infrastructure.

89
00:03:47,333 --> 00:03:49,600
P4U invited strangers and non

90
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:52,267
professional makers to bring proposals,

91
00:03:52,267 --> 00:03:55,733
form temporary groups and make work together.

92
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:57,133
Each edition could change

93
00:03:57,133 --> 00:03:58,867
with the people who entered it.

94
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,567
Cocoon transformed an open call and sixteen

95
00:04:04,567 --> 00:04:06,533
days of rehearsal into dance theatre

96
00:04:06,533 --> 00:04:09,367
Built from bodies and participant experience.

97
00:04:09,367 --> 00:04:12,033
Howlers on the Rooftop moved through writing,

98
00:04:12,033 --> 00:04:13,667
training, performance,

99
00:04:13,667 --> 00:04:15,267
discussion, and seven

100
00:04:15,267 --> 00:04:17,067
behind the scenes accounts.

101
00:04:17,333 --> 00:04:19,967
Centrist extended performance into auditions,

102
00:04:19,967 --> 00:04:22,433
rehearsal, surveillance, images,

103
00:04:22,433 --> 00:04:24,967
interviews, and after texts.

104
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:28,167
Participation was not added after the show.

105
00:04:28,167 --> 00:04:29,967
It shaped the work's structure,

106
00:04:29,967 --> 00:04:32,000
memory, and public life.

107
00:04:32,067 --> 00:04:33,967
In Purple Action and Duel Club,

108
00:04:33,967 --> 00:04:36,000
rules, votes, players,

109
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,400
spectators, and shared consequences

110
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:40,833
formed temporary political structures.

111
00:04:40,833 --> 00:04:43,433
P4 tried to redistribute authorship,

112
00:04:43,433 --> 00:04:45,233
while preserving the cost:

113
00:04:45,233 --> 00:04:46,733
Conflict, rupture,

114
00:04:46,733 --> 00:04:49,233
abandoned plans, and criticism.

115
00:04:49,233 --> 00:04:50,500
Failure becomes evidence

116
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:51,933
for the next experiment.

117
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,600
After leaving the original venue in 2021,

118
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,567
P4 moved through parks,

119
00:04:56,567 --> 00:04:58,467
boxing rings, offices,

120
00:04:58,467 --> 00:05:00,633
dance studios, bookstores,

121
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:03,700
ruins, and temporary public spaces.

122
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:06,233
The next fixed site was a room of roughly

123
00:05:06,233 --> 00:05:07,700
sixteen square metres,

124
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:09,633
known as 510.

125
00:05:09,633 --> 00:05:12,167
There, actors, cameras,

126
00:05:12,167 --> 00:05:14,367
objects, and viewers could not

127
00:05:14,367 --> 00:05:15,933
remain separated.

128
00:05:15,933 --> 00:05:18,167
Iceberg developed through meetings,

129
00:05:18,167 --> 00:05:21,200
rehearsals, field filming, interviews,

130
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:23,600
performance, and criticism.

131
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,833
The project was no longer only a show,

132
00:05:25,833 --> 00:05:27,367
but a network.

133
00:05:27,367 --> 00:05:29,233
P4 was becoming less

134
00:05:29,233 --> 00:05:30,933
a building than an ecology.

135
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,367
In 2023, Human Surrender

136
00:05:33,367 --> 00:05:35,333
pushed this system into cinema.

137
00:05:35,333 --> 00:05:37,900
Its recruitment proposed a chamber film,

138
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:39,300
observation of performers’

139
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:42,400
daily lives and a public performance.

140
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:44,733
The Last Rehearsal combined theatre,

141
00:05:44,733 --> 00:05:45,933
performance art,

142
00:05:45,933 --> 00:05:47,067
live sound,

143
00:05:47,067 --> 00:05:49,933
installation and continuous filming.

144
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,233
Audience actions could enter the film.

145
00:05:52,233 --> 00:05:53,933
Actors could direct.

146
00:05:53,933 --> 00:05:55,833
Camera operators perform,

147
00:05:55,833 --> 00:05:57,833
observers become agents.

148
00:05:57,833 --> 00:06:00,000
The camera entered the event.

149
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
The 2024 film

150
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,367
Shoot Self with You makes “with you” central:

151
00:06:05,367 --> 00:06:07,667
a self appears through another person,

152
00:06:07,667 --> 00:06:09,933
a camera and a later viewer.

153
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,467
P4's archive does not freeze the work.

154
00:06:14,467 --> 00:06:16,067
It keeps sources, dates,

155
00:06:16,067 --> 00:06:18,633
arguments, and memories in relation.

156
00:06:18,633 --> 00:06:21,133
One experiment generates the next.

157
00:06:21,133 --> 00:06:24,633
P4 is not an answer, but an invitation.

158
00:06:24,633 --> 00:06:27,633
Theatre is not an end point, but a beginning.

